"173900;track:impression,attention" data-hveid="1"><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c757676767="" class="response-container-header ng-tns-c757676767-1255 ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c757676767="" class="response-container-header-controls ng-tns-c757676767-1255"><div _ngcontent-ng-c757676767="" class="ng-tns-c757676767-1255 tts ng-trigger ng-trigger-singleResponseEnter ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c757676767="" class="single-draft-response-container ng-tns-c757676767-1255"><!----></div></div><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c757676767="" class="response-container-header-status ng-tns-c757676767-1255"><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c757676767="" class="response-container-header-processing-state ng-tns-c757676767-1255"></div></div></div><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c757676767="" class="presented-response-container ng-tns-c757676767-1255" jslog="283401;track:impression,attention" data-hveid="2"><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c757676767="" class="response-container-content ng-tns-c757676767-1255"><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c551107045="" highlighttoaskhost="" class="response-content ng-tns-c757676767-1255"><!----><!----><thinking-overlay _ngcontent-ng-c551107045="" _nghost-ng-c2956030567="" class="enable-luminous-fast-follows ng-star-inserted"><!----></thinking-overlay><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c551107045="" class="model-response-label-announcer" aria-busy="false" aria-live="off"><!----><!----><h6 _ngcontent-ng-c551107045="" class="cdk-visually-hidden screen-reader-model-response-label ng-star-inserted" style="">Gemini said</h6><!----><!----></div><!----><model-response-content _ngcontent-ng-c551107045="" _nghost-ng-c305644972=""><!----><structured-content-container _ngcontent-ng-c305644972="" class="model-response-text processing-state-visible ng-star-inserted" _nghost-ng-c861632216="" style="height: auto;"><div _ngcontent-ng-c861632216="" class="container"><message-content _ngcontent-ng-c861632216="" _nghost-ng-c1987417986="" id="message-content-id-r_2d831a81ef34157a" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c1987417986="" inline-copy-host="" class="markdown markdown-main-panel md-content enable-luminous-fast-follows enable-updated-hr-color tutor-markdown-rendering" id="model-response-message-contentr_2d831a81ef34157a" aria-busy="false" aria-live="off" dir="ltr" style="--animation-duration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: ease-out;"><p dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="0" id="p-rc_5d68b1f61436f1a2-166"><span data-path-to-node="0,0">That "Compare &amp; pull request" button appears on GitHub because your local branch (<code data-path-to-node="0,0" data-index-in-node="82">security-tool</code>) is ahead of the <code data-path-to-node="0,0" data-index-in-node="113">main</code> branch by 1 commit</span><span data-path-to-node="0,1"><span><response-element class="no-md" ng-version="0.0.0-PLACEHOLDER"><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><source-footnote _nghost-ng-c2821379991="" class="ng-star-inserted"><sup _ngcontent-ng-c2821379991="" class="superscript"><!----></sup></source-footnote><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></response-element></span></span><span data-path-to-node="0,2">, and GitHub is offering to help you merge those changes back into <code data-path-to-node="0,2" data-index-in-node="67">main</code>.</span><sources-carousel-inline ng-version="0.0.0-PLACEHOLDER" _nghost-ng-c2769209970="">   <!----><source-inline-chip _ngcontent-ng-c2769209970="" _nghost-ng-c3622118488="" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c3622118488="" class="source-inline-chip-container luminous-sources hide-from-message-actions ng-star-inserted"><button _ngcontent-ng-c3622118488="" cdkoverlayorigin="" class="button multiple-button ng-star-inserted" aria-label="View source details for citation from JPG: media-87E93049-B2C9-473C-A2B6-DD361DA33DF5.jpg. Press Enter to open sources dialogue." aria-expanded="false" aria-haspopup="dialog" jslog="262206;track:generic_click,impression,attention" data-hveid="3"><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c3622118488="" dir="auto" class="source-label-container gds-body-s ng-star-inserted"><!----><span _ngcontent-ng-c3622118488="" class="source-title" style="max-width: 20ch;">media-87E93049-B2C9-473C-A2B6-DD361DA33DF5.jpg</span><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----></button><!----><!----><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></source-inline-chip><!----><!----><!----></sources-carousel-inline></p><p dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="1">Here is what that button actually means and what you should do with it:</p><ul dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="2"><li><p dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="2,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="2,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">What it does:</b> A Pull Request (PR) is a request to merge the code from your feature branch (<code data-path-to-node="2,0,0" data-index-in-node="91">security-tool</code>) into your main branch (<code data-path-to-node="2,0,0" data-index-in-node="129">main</code>). Because you are working on a cybersecurity coursework project with multiple distinct tasks, you usually keep each task on its own separate branch until the entire coursework is finished.</p></li><li><p dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="2,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="2,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">What you should do right now:</b> <b data-path-to-node="2,1,0" data-index-in-node="30">Leave it alone for now!</b> You don't need to click it yet. Since you are about to start <b data-path-to-node="2,1,0" data-index-in-node="115">Task 2</b> on a brand-new branch (<code data-path-to-node="2,1,0" data-index-in-node="145">security-event-logger</code>), you will eventually have multiple branches (<code data-path-to-node="2,1,0" data-index-in-node="213">security-tool</code>, <code data-path-to-node="2,1,0" data-index-in-node="228">security-event-logger</code>, etc.). Students often keep them separate or merge them only when instructed by their coursework guidelines.</p></li></ul><div class="attachment-container unknown md-has-block-component"><response-element class="no-md" ng-version="0.0.0-PLACEHOLDER"><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><follow-up _nghost-ng-c1795396892="" class="lm-enabled ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c1795396892="" hide-from-message-actions="" class="follow-up-container hide-from-message-actions"><div _ngcontent-ng-c1795396892="" class="follow-up-text gds-headline-s">Ready to create your Task 2 branch and start coding?</div><div _ngcontent-ng-c1795396892="" class="follow-up-button-container"><button _ngcontent-ng-c1795396892="" class="follow-up-button lm-enabled ng-star-inserted" jslog="270376;track:generic_click"><gem-icon _ngcontent-ng-c1795396892="" fonticonname="prompt_suggestion" size="small" _nghost-ng-c4096424917=""><mat-icon _ngcontent-ng-c4096424917="" role="img" class="mat-icon notranslate lm-icon-s lumi-symbols mat-ligature-font mat-icon-no-color ng-star-inserted" aria-hidden="true" data-mat-icon-type="font" data-mat-icon-name="prompt_suggestion" data-mat-icon-namespace="lumi-symbols" fonticon="prompt_suggestion"></mat-icon><!----><!----><!----></gem-icon><span _ngcontent-ng-c1795396892="" class="gds-body-m">Yes</span></button><!----><!----></div></div></follow-up><!----><!----><!----><!----><!--