-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #for loop is used to iterate 10 times, which corresponds to the maximum number of password attempts allowed. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; pw=input("Password: ") <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The input() function is used to prompt the user to enter a password. The entered password is stored in the variable pw. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; if pw != "secret": <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #If the entered password is not equal to the string "secret", it means the password attempt <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; incorrect=incorrect+1 <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The variable incorrect is incremented by 1 to keep track of the number of incorrect password attempts made by the user. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><br _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----><!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; print("total incorrect", incorrect) <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; #The print() function is used to display the total number of incorrect password attempts made by the user after all 10 attempts have been completed. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; if incorrect &gt; 5: <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #If the total number of incorrect password attempts is greater than 5, it means that the user has made more than 50% incorrect attempts. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; print("ALERT: over 50% incorrect") <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The print() function is used to display an alert message indicating that the user has made more than 50% incorrect password attempts. This serves as a warning to the user about their performance in entering the correct password. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><br _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----><!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> def brute_force(): <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; #function to simulate a brute-force password guessing attempt <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; attempts=0 <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; #variable attempts is initialized to 0. This variable will be used to keep track of the number of password guessing attempts made by the user. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><br _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----><!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; while attempts &lt;3: <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The while loop is used to allow the user to make password guessing attempts until the maximum number of attempts (3) is reached. The loop will continue as long as the value of attempts is less than 3. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; guess=input("password guess: ") <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The input() function is used to prompt the user to enter a password guess. The entered guess is stored in the variable guess. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; attempts=attempts+1 <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The variable attempts is incremented by 1 to keep track of the number of password guessing attempts made by the user. This ensures that the loop will eventually terminate after 3 attempts. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><br _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----><!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; if guess=="secret": <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #If the entered password guess is equal to the string "secret", <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; print("success!") <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The print() function is used to display a success message indicating that the user has correctly guessed the password. This serves as feedback to the user that their guess was correct. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; return <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #If the entered password guess is not equal to the string "secret <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><br _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----><!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; print("Max amount of attempts reached") <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; #The print() function is used to display a message indicating that the maximum number of password guessing attempts has been reached. This serves as feedback to the user that they have exhausted their allowed attempts and can no longer make further guesses. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><br _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----><!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> def login(): <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; #function to simulate a login process with a maximum of 3 attempts <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp;  <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; failed=0 <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; #variable failed is initialized to 0. This variable will be used to keep track of the number of failed login attempts made by the user. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><br _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----><!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; while failed &lt;3: <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The while loop is used to allow the user to make login attempts until the maximum number of failed attempts (3) is reached. The loop will continue as long as the value of failed is less than 3. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; user=input("username: ") <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The input() function is used to prompt the user to enter a username. The entered username is stored in the variable user. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; pw=input("password: ") <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The input() function is used to prompt the user to enter a password. The entered password is stored in the variable pw. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; if user=="admin" and pw =="secret": <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #If the entered username is equal to the string "admin" and the entered password is equal to the string "secret", it means that <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; print("success!") <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The print() function is used to display a success message indicating that the user has successfully logged in. This serves as feedback to the user that their login credentials were correct. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; return <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #If the entered username and password do not match the expected values, it means that the login attempt has failed. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; else: <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The else statement is executed when the login attempt fails. It indicates that the entered username and password do not match the expected values. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; failed=failed+1 <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The variable failed is incremented by 1 to keep track of the number of failed login attempts made by the user. This ensures that the loop will eventually terminate after 3 failed attempts. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><br _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----><!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; print("account is forzen for 24 hours") <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; #The print() function is used to display a message indicating that the account is frozen for 24 hours. This serves as feedback to the user that they have exceeded the maximum number of allowed login attempts and will not be able to access the account for a specified period of time. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><br _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----><!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> def main(): <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; #function to simulate a security tool with multiple options for the user to choose from <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; while True: <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The while loop is used to create an infinite loop that will continue until the user chooses to exit the program. This allows the user to repeatedly access the different options available in the security tool. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; user=input("startup user: ") <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The input() function is used to prompt the user to enter a username for the startup login process. The entered username is stored in the variable user. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; pw=input("startup pass: ") <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The input() function is used to prompt the user to enter a password for the startup login process. The entered password is stored in the variable pw. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; if user=="admin" and pw=="secret": <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #If the entered username is equal to the string "admin" and the entered password is equal to the string "secret", it means that the startup <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; print("startup login successful!\n") <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The print() function is used to display a success message indicating that the startup login was successful. This serves as feedback to the user that their login credentials were correct and they can proceed to access the security tool. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; break <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #If the entered username and password do not match the expected values, it means that the startup login attempt has failed. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><br _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----><!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; while True: <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The while loop is used to create an infinite loop that will continue until the user chooses to exit the program. This allows the user to repeatedly access the different options available in the security tool. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; choice=input("\n1.counter\n2. brute-force\n3. login\n4. exit\nchoice: ") <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The input() function is used to prompt the user to enter their choice from the available options in the security tool. The entered choice is stored in the variable choice. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><br _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----><!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; if choice =="1": <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The if statement checks if the user's choice is equal to the string "1", which corresponds to the option for the event counter functionality in the security tool. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; event_counter() <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The event_counter() function is called to execute the event counter functionality. This function will count the number of incorrect password attempts made by the user and provide feedback accordingly. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; elif choice =="2": <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The elif statement checks if the user's choice is equal to the string "2", which corresponds to the option for the brute-force password guessing functionality in the security tool. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; brute_force() <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The brute_force() function is called to execute the brute-force password guessing functionality. This function will allow the user to make password guessing attempts and provide feedback on their success or failure. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; elif choice =="3": <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The elif statement checks if the user's choice is equal to the string "3", which corresponds to the option for the login functionality in the security tool. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; login() <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The login() function is called to execute the login functionality. This function will allow the user to attempt to log in with a username and password, providing feedback on their success or failure. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; elif choice=="4": <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The elif statement checks if the user's choice is equal to the string "4", which corresponds to the option to exit the security tool. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; print("thank you for using the security tool") <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The print() function is used to display a thank you message to the user for using the security tool. This serves as a polite farewell message before exiting the program. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; break <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The break statement is used to exit the while loop, effectively terminating the program and ending the execution of the security tool. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; else: <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The else statement is executed when the user's choice does not match any of the available options in the security tool. It indicates that the entered choice is invalid. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; print("Invalid choice. try again") <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; #The print() function is used to display an error message indicating that the user's choice is invalid. This serves as feedback to the user, prompting them to enter a valid option from the available choices in the security tool. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><br _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----><!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> if __name__ == "__main__": <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; #The if __name__ == "__main__": statement checks if the script is being run directly (as opposed to being imported as a module). If it is being run directly, it calls the main() function to execute the program. <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" dir="auto" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----> &nbsp; &nbsp; main() <!----><!----></p><!----><!----><!----><!----></div><!----></span><div _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" class="luminous-toggle-container ng-star-inserted"><!----><button _ngcontent-ng-c3142143690="" mat-icon-button="" theme="lm" aria-expanded="true" aria-label="Collapse" gemtooltip="Collapse text" data-test-id="luminous-collapse-button" class="mdc-icon-button mat-mdc-icon-button mat-mdc-button-base mat-mdc-tooltip-trigger luminous-toggle-button mat-unthemed _mat-animation-noopable lm-enabled ng-star-inserted" mat-ripple-loader-class-name="mat-mdc-button-ripple" mat-ripple-loader-centered="" jslog="224551;track:generic_click,impression;BardVeMetadataKey:W1sicl83MDhhYzkyNjMzYTdlOTQ2IiwiY182NGE3ZWY5ZDBhNzI3Y2M0IixudWxsLG51bGwsbnVsbCxudWxsLG51bGwsbnVsbCwxLG51bGwsbnVsbCxudWxsLDBdXQ