<span class="hljs-section">## Program Overview</span>
for task 2 i made a security event logger in python that continuously asks the user to enter a username and password until they get it right. for every single try—whether it fails or succeeds—the program generates and prints out a detailed event log showing a random 4-digit event ID, the entered username, the system IP address, the event status (failed or successful login), and an exact timestamp.

<span class="hljs-section">## Code Logic &amp; Features Used</span>
i used several built-in python libraries and control flow structures. i imported the random module and used random.randint(1000, 9999) to generate a unique 4-digit event ID for every attempt. i imported the datetime module to capture the current date and time and formatted it into a readable string using strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S"). i imported the socket module to connect to a public address and fetch the local system's ip address, and wrapped it in a try-except block so that if there is a network error it gracefully falls back to 127.0.0.1. for control flow, i used a while true loop to keep the login prompt running continuously on incorrect attempts, and an if/else statement to check credentials, update the event status, and break out of the loop with a success message when correct login details are provided.

<span class="hljs-section">## How to Run</span>
open in your terminal in the repository folder. make sure you are on the security-event-logger branch. run the script using "bash"
python security<span class="hljs-emphasis">_event_</span>logger.py

<span class="hljs-section">## Terminal Output Screenshot</span>
![<span class="hljs-string">Task 2 Output</span>](<span class="hljs-link">task2_output.png</span>)
