d="code-content" class="code-container formatted ng-tns-c1049210364-1349"><span class="hljs-section"># Name: Haseeb Amir Rasool | Campus: New College Lanarkshire | ID: B01887873</span>

<span class="hljs-section">## Program Overview</span>

for task 2 i made a security event logger in 
python that keeps asking the user for a username 
and password until they get it right. for every 
single try—whether it fails or succeeds—the program 
prints out a log showing a random 4-digit event ID, 
the username, the ip address, the login status, 
and the exact timestamp.

<span class="hljs-section">## Code Logic &amp; Features Used</span>

i used several modules for this program. i imported 
the random module and used random.randint(1000, 9999) 
to make a random 4-digit event ID for every try. i 
imported the datetime module with datetime.now().
strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S") to get the current date 
and time formatted nicely as a string. 

for getting the ip address, i imported the socket module 
and connected to a public dns server to grab the system's 
local ip. i put this inside a try-except block so that 
if there is any network error, it won't crash the program 
and will just fall back to 127.0.0.1 instead. 

for control flow, i used a while true loop to keep the 
login prompt running continuously until the correct admin 
credentials are entered, using if/else statements to 
check everything and break out of the loop on success.

<span class="hljs-section">## How to Run</span>

open your terminal in the repository folder. 
make sure you are on the security-event-logger branch. 
run the script using:
python security<span class="hljs-emphasis">_event_</span>logger.py

<span class="hljs-section">## Terminal Output Screenshot</span>

![<span class="hljs-string">Task 2 Output</span>](<span class="hljs-link">task2_output.png</span>)
