g-c1987417986="" inline-copy-host="" class="markdown markdown-main-panel md-content enable-luminous-fast-follows enable-updated-hr-color tutor-markdown-rendering" id="model-response-message-contentr_aa42c8fe1dbdccb7" aria-busy="false" aria-live="polite" dir="ltr" style="--animation-duration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: ease-out;"><p dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="0" class="first-token" style="--animation-duration: 450ms;"><span class="">To test Task 2 properly according to typical NCFE cybersecurity coursework requirements,</span><span> you want to prove that your script handles </span><b data-path-to-node="0" data-index-in-node="132">both</b><span> failed and successful login attempts correctly,</span><span> logs the randomized ID,</span><span> fetches the IP,</span><span> and captures the timestamp.</span></p><p dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="1"><span>Here is how you should test it step-by-step in your terminal:</span></p><ol start="1" dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="2" class="md-has-block-component"><li><p dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="2,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="2,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Open your terminal</b><span> in VS Code and make sure you are on your </span><code data-path-to-node="2,0,0" data-index-in-node="60">security-event-logger</code><span> branch.</span></p></li><li><p dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="2,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="2,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Run your script:</b></p><response-element class="no-md" ng-version="0.0.0-PLACEHOLDER"><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><code-block _nghost-ng-c1049210364="" class="ng-tns-c1049210364-1353 enable-luminous-code-block ng-star-inserted" style=""><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c1049210364="" class="code-block ng-tns-c1049210364-1353 ng-animate-disabled ng-trigger ng-trigger-codeBlockRevealAnimation" jslog="223238;track:impression,attention;BardVeMetadataKey:W1sicl9hYTQyYzhmZTFkYmRjY2I3IiwiY182NGE3ZWY5ZDBhNzI3Y2M0IixudWxsLCJyY182MTg0MTQxZGU1MTc1NTVhIixudWxsLG51bGwsImVuIixudWxsLDEsbnVsbCxud